      ":question/id": "7cb31f11-b810-5cc6-992c-c0b4ae3a3569",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $-2\\sqrt{7}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{2}{8}=-\\frac{1}{4}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-62$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{25}=5$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-\\frac{2}{8}$; $-62$."
